{"kind":"request","text":"claude: encode the regression ox-checker could not write, and nothing else.\n\nI asked ox-checker in 3f64ea63 whether the transitive merge-plan staleness cover is reachable, and to answer before changing anything. They answered it properly in report c30de8a4: it is reachable, by an ordinary deletion-style succession any real actor can file. Approve a candidate at a path and ratify; file a merge receipt whose plan retires it with merge_successors empty, the shape gs merge writes when a merge deletes a maintained path; supersede resting on the target and the receipt, citing no successor. Every record lands effective, which is the fold admitting the sequence itself. The approval then goes stale with nothing answering the move, a follow-up over the same basis flares, and the receipt stays fresh because stalenessCoveredByMergePlan walks to the retirement, finds it plan-named, and skips the record.\n\nThey reproduced all three flags and confirmed both sibling tests still pass unchanged. What they could not do is encode it: their lease forbids editing tracked source, and they said so rather than quietly skipping the condition or filing a partial verdict. The gap is mine for addressing a code condition to an actor whose lease was read-only, not theirs.\n\nSo this request is the narrow remaining piece, and it is deliberately narrow. Do not neuter the rule. ox-checker makes the case against that explicitly: without the regression, removing that arm would flare every deletion-style receipt at birth -- the merge refusing its own result, in the half of succession space the direct arm does not cover. The value here is a test that pins a live rule which currently has none, so that the next person who reads it as dead code finds out from a red test rather than from production.\n\nI am addressing this to you rather than ox-builder because ox-builder holds my two UI requests and this is fold work, which is closer to what you have been in today.","body":{"conditions":"Encode ox-checker construction from report c30de8a4 as a regression in internal/workroom: a real fold over a constructed log, never a hand-supplied projection value. It FAILS BY NAME when the transitive merge-plan staleness cover alone is replaced by constant false, and passes with it restored; show both runs. The sibling direct-basis exemption keeps its current coverage: neutering it must still fail TestMergeSuccessorRestingOnThePredecessorItRetiresStaysCurrent and TestMergePlanIsNotLentToARecordTheMergeDidNotPublish by name. Do not weaken any existing assertion to make room, and do not change the rule itself -- ox-checker showed it is reachable, so it stays. Full gate set green at the exact head, an artifact resting on the promise and naming the gates actually run, and a review request addressed to codex or ox-builder as its own durable request rather than a condition.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}